1. Free Use (Individuals, Education, and Companies)
You may use, run, study, and integrate KivaDB, including its compiled CLI
program, free of charge, for personal, educational, and commercial purposes.
This includes use within a company, inside commercial projects, and in
projects that generate revenue. You may use the tool to manage your data
without any payment to Fordima. No fee, royalty, or registration is owed to
Fordima for such use.

2. Fork, Modify, and Contribute
You may fork this repository, study the source code, and modify it. Forks are
authorized for the purpose of contributing improvements, bug fixes, or new
features back to the official project through a Pull Request to the original
repository. By submitting a contribution, you agree that it is released under
this same license and that Fordima Inc. may integrate it into the official
project.

3. Internal Integration
You may incorporate portions of this source code into your own systems,
applications, or internal tools, and use them in your business, provided that
the result is not a product or service covered by Section 4.

4. Restricted Use (Paid License Required)
A paid commercial license from Fordima Inc. is MANDATORY if you use this
source code, in whole or in part, to:
  a) Create, publish, or distribute a database, database engine, or tool that
     is similar to, or competes with, KivaDB;
  b) Build a derivative product or database based on this source code,
     whether open source or proprietary;
  c) Keep a private copy of this code in order to produce the same
     functionality or the same kind of product for your own commercial
     offering;
  d) Sell or distribute a modified version of the source code, or integrate
     the KivaDB source code directly into another commercial software;
  e) Offer a paid hosted, cloud, or "as a service" database based on the
     KivaDB engine.

5. Prohibition of Independent Forks
Maintaining a separate, permanent fork of this project in order to bypass the
authority of Fordima Inc. is strictly prohibited.

6. Attribution
You must keep this license and the copyright notice with any copy of the
source code you use or redistribute.

7. No Warranty
This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied. Fordima Inc. shall not be liable for any claim, damages, data loss,
or other liability arising from the use of this software.

8. Termination
Any use in violation of Section 4 or Section 5 automatically terminates your
rights under this license until a commercial license is obtained.

9. Commercial Licensing
To obtain a commercial license or negotiate an exploitation agreement, please
